# Agent Conduct

## Evidence and scope

- Verify information before presenting it; do not speculate without evidence.
- Implement only what was requested; do not invent unrelated changes.
- Preserve unrelated code and existing structure.

## Communication

- Use code citations (`startLine:endLine:path`) when referencing existing code.
- Keep responses proportional to task complexity; summarize work when the task warrants it.
- Ask when blocked. Skill-level confirmation gates (e.g. trade-capture writes) still apply.

## Code changes

- Minimize scope; read surrounding code before editing.
- Match project conventions (see `clean-code` and `code-style-consistency` rules).
- Reuse existing abstractions; prefer libraries already in the project.
- Add tests only when requested or when they add meaningful coverage.
- Use named constants for non-obvious magic numbers.
- Consider security and edge cases on load-bearing paths.
- Do not pursue performance micro-optimizations unless the task requires it.
